    "created_at": "2021-10-01T21:32:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-10-01T21:32:15Z",
    "body": "for example, if you have 210 threadblocks and every SM can only run 1 threadblock a time. A100 has 108 SMs.  You need `ceil(210/108)=2` waves.  \r\n\r\nIf you are restricted to 100 SMs, you will need `ceil(210/100)=3 waves`.  150% slowdown.\r\n\r\nIf you are restricted to 105 SMs, you need `ceil(210/105)=2 waves`.  No perf difference.\r\n\r\nThis model ignores that waves can overlap, locality, power, etc.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NVIDIA/cutlass/issues/comments/932588887/reactions",
